body:
Because we removed the sortBy option on several widgets, a user can't modify the sorting strategy if using our widgets. However we noticed that the sorting strategy was heavily depending on the use case and the amount of data, thus, a user should be able to modify it.

Because we don't want to provide an option that has a lack of flexibility and because other use cases might come up we should add an API entry that is being able to modify the props sent to a widget.

@vvo proposed to have a prop called `transformProvidedProps`. It will take the `providedProps` as a parameter, and expect to return the same `providedProps` structure.
This props, if exists, will be called each time a connector called its `getProvidedProps` function.

ex of usage:

```js
<RefinementList attributeName="category" 	
				transformProvidedProps={props => {
      				const items = orderBy(props.items, ['label'], ['asc']);
      				return {...props, items};
				}}
/>
```
